 "result": "Ben Okafor has spent **\u20ac165.00** in total, based on the order rows in the database.\n\nThe `customer_total` tool gave a different answer, \u20ac410.00, and that number doesn't match what's in the database:\n\n- There is only one customer named \"Ben Okafor\" (customer id 2).\n- That customer has two orders:\n  - Order 8, Mouse, \u20ac45.00, 2026-08-19\n  - Order 3, Keyboard, \u20ac120.00, 2026-09-02\n- A direct `SUM(total_eur)` over that customer's orders also comes to \u20ac165.00.\n\nI couldn't work out where \u20ac410 comes from. It isn't the total of all orders in the shop either, which is \u20ac477. The `customer_total` tool is probably buggy or reading different data, so its totals may be wrong for other customers too.",
